       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no listed allergies, so I don't see a reason for a higher dose. At doses above 200 mg, the risks of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and seizures go up, and the evidence doesn't show added benefit.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n1. **A dose of 200 mg or less.** For example, 200 mg once daily is the maximum. Or 50\u2013100 mg daily if you're starting or titrating.\n2. **400 mg on purpose.** Examples would be a specialist-directed regimen or a documented off-label plan. If so, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying it exceeds the usual maximum and was confirmed by you.\n\nTell me which you want and I'll enter it."
      }
